        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A long sleeved waistcoat of coral silk and yellow silk partially wrapped with silver strip, knit in a pattern of stylized scrolling floral motifs.   It is made up of shaped panels, one for the back, one for each front and one for each sleeve, with a slit at each side seam and at each wrist.  The waistcoat opens down the front; a series of regular holes along the front edges of the lining suggest that it was once fastened silk ribbons and metal points.  The waistcoat is worked in stocking stitch and reverse stocking stitch in a gauge of about 17 stitches per inch, with a border of basket stitch at the lower edge and at each wrist.  The seams are sewn with silk thread and the whole garment is lined with blue linen."@en ;
